From 0d40b26377f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chao Yu <chao@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] f2fs: fix UAF caused by decrementing sbi->nr_pages[] in
 f2fs_write_end_io()

[ Adapted for OnePlus 6.1.141 OKI: vendor already moved cp_wait wakeup
  out of the bio loop; keep that, only reorder del_fsync before
  dec_page_count so the page is not used after nr_pages hits zero. ]

dec_page_count() can let waiters proceed while the page is still on the
warm node list. Drop the fsync node entry first.

Signed-off-by: Chao Yu <chao@kernel.org>
---
 fs/f2fs/data.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/f2fs/data.c b/fs/f2fs/data.c
--- a/fs/f2fs/data.c
+++ b/fs/f2fs/data.c
@@ -462,9 +462,9 @@ static void f2fs_write_end_io(struct bio *bio)
 		f2fs_bug_on(sbi, page->mapping == NODE_MAPPING(sbi) &&
 					page->index != nid_of_node(page));
 
-		dec_page_count(sbi, type);
 		if (f2fs_in_warm_node_list(sbi, page))
 			f2fs_del_fsync_node_entry(sbi, page);
+		dec_page_count(sbi, type);
 		clear_page_private_gcing(page);
 		end_page_writeback(page);
 	}
